{
"dur": 56.42,
"shots": [
{
"i": 1,
"start": 0.0,
"vo_start": 0.6,
"vo_end": 4.131,
"text": "Two days later, the meat runs low. Today you hunt.",
"end": 4.406
},
{
"i": 2,
"start": 4.406,
"vo_start": 4.681,
"vo_end": 13.1,
"text": "Some hunters in Africa have been recorded using a method that looks nothing like the movies. They don't try to outrun the animal. They can't.",
"end": 13.375
},
{
"i": 3,
"start": 13.375,
"vo_start": 13.65,
"vo_end": 17.41,
"text": "Instead they track it, at a steady pace, for hours, in the midday heat.",
"end": 17.685
},
{
"i": 4,
"start": 17.685,
"vo_start": 17.96,
"vo_end": 26.39,
"text": "A human can sweat and keep cooling while moving. A four-legged runner has to stop to pant. Push it hard enough, for long enough, and it overheats.",
"end": 26.665
},
{
"i": 5,
"start": 26.665,
"vo_start": 26.94,
"vo_end": 31.712,
"text": "Eventually the animal stops and can't run again. The hunters walk up to it.",
"end": 31.987
},
{
"i": 6,
"start": 31.987,
"vo_start": 32.262,
"vo_end": 36.54,
"text": "You were never the fastest thing on the plain. You were the thing that could keep going.",
"end": 36.815
},
{
"i": 7,
"start": 36.815,
"vo_start": 37.09,
"vo_end": 44.97,
"text": "This is called persistence hunting, and it's only one method among many. Most hunts used traps, snares, ambush and poisoned arrows.",
"end": 45.245
},
{
"i": 8,
"start": 45.245,
"vo_start": 45.52,
"vo_end": 52.52,
"text": "A big hunt can take the whole day, and it's the hardest work this life asks for. But one good kill feeds the camp for days.",
"end": 52.795
},
{
"i": 9,
"start": 52.795,
"vo_start": 53.07,
"vo_end": 55.47,
"text": "So tomorrow, the free time comes back.",
"end": 56.42
}
],
